Fix hardware-encoder CSD handling for video compression (Samsung devices).

MediaCodec encoders can hand the interaction of CSD and inline parameter
sets through packets such that extract_extradata collects SPS/PPS twice;
the container header written from that pool then carries duplicated
parameter-set entries, and muxers like FLV rewrite a second, different
header whenever later packets re-supply sets. Two conflicting header
snapshots in one file: linear playback survives on the clean inline
copies, but players that reconfigure the decoder from the container
header on a seek or surface change initialize from the wrong snapshot —
FLV black screens and MKV/MOV seek/resume freezes on real devices.

This patch:
 1. normalizes every CSD where it enters the encoder wrapper into one
    Annex B copy of each parameter set (dedupes repeated SPS/PPS, and
    also accepts avcC/hvcC-shaped vendor CSDs),
 2. normalizes the dummy-frame NEW_EXTRADATA side data before it
    becomes the global header,
 3. strips parameter-set NALs from output packets whenever a global
    header already carries them (H264/HEVC), so extract_extradata never
    re-fires and the header stays the single source of truth.

